  - packages/gnomon/src/kernel/log/replay.ts
  - packages/gnomon/src/cli/replay-cli.ts
  - packages/gnomon/test/m112-replay.test.ts
learnings:
  - A read-only WAL reader's statement snapshot already excludes rows committed after it began; the test commits a row from inside the verify pass (a KeyRing subclass) and the projection hash is unchanged
  - Kernel and peer injects are folded as inputs but never matched to a turn; only origin:client feeds session.send
  - The replay buffers the verified rows until verify reports ok (memory grows with log size; a streaming fold that discards on failure is the follow-up)
